       "id": "math11-u4-c01",
       "type": "text",
       "title": "Exponential Functions",
       "page": 142,
       "src": "notes",
       "body": [
        "An exponential function is f(x)=b^x with b>0 and b not 1. If b>1 it grows. If 0<b<1 it decays. The graph passes through (0,1)."
       ]
      },
      {
       "id": "math11-u4-c02",
       "type": "mnemonic",
       "title": "Change of base",
       "page": 142,
       "src": "notes",
       "body": [
        "log_a b = log b / log a. Use the same base on top and bottom."
       ]
      },
      {
       "id": "math11-u4-c03",
       "type": "worked",
       "title": "Worked example",
       "page": 142,
       "src": "notes",
       "problem": "Solve 2^x=32 and log_2(x-1)=3.",
       "steps": [
        {
         "text": "32=2^5, so x=5."
        },
        {
         "text": "log_2(x-1)=3 means x-1=8, so x=9. Check that x-1 is positive."
        }
       ],
       "answer": "x=5 and x=9"
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "title": "Exponential & log",
       "page": 1,
       "body": [
        "aˣ grows/decays; log_a is inverse. log_a(xy)=log_a x+log_a y; log_a(x/y)=log_a x−log_a y; log_a(xⁿ)=n log_a x.",
        "Change of base: log_a x = ln x / ln a."
       ],
       "id": "math11-u4-deep1"
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "title": "Growth & decay models",
       "body": [
        "A=A₀e^(kt) or A₀(1+r)^t. k>0 growth, k<0 decay.",
        "Half-life: amount halves when exponent hits ln(1/2)."
       ],
       "id": "math11-u4-xtra1",
       "page": 1
      },
